THE_RETRACTION.IT_IS_WRONG:
RunHistoricalScoreExport's excursion loop BREAKS the moment the SHIPPED bracket resolves:
    for(int f = bar-1; f >= MathMax(0, bar-20); f--) {
        if(_favExc > _mfeATR) { _mfeATR = _favExc; ... }
        if(isLong) { if(High[f]>=tp){won=true;resolved=true;break;} if(Low[f]<=sl){resolved=true;break;} }
    }
So mfe_atr and mae_atr do NOT describe the trade's run. They describe it only up to the point the shipped exit closed it. A trade stopped out at bar 3 has its favourable excursion frozen at bar 3 -- the move it would have made under a WIDER stop was never recorded. Using those columns to evaluate a wider bracket is therefore invalid by construction, and the +0.19 is truncation, not edge.
